    # @param price_max [Float] Only offers priced at or below this many yuan (CNY).
    # @param province [String] Only suppliers in this Chinese province, by its Chinese name,
    # e.g. 广东 (Guangdong), 浙江 (Zhejiang), 江苏 (Jiangsu).
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'DE',
    # 'SG'). Leave blank to let the API pick.
    # Calls POST /marketplace/1688-search.
    def alibaba1688_search(q, page: nil, max_results: nil, sort: nil, price_min: nil, price_max: nil, province: nil, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/1688-search", {
        q: q,
        page: page,
        max_results: max_results,
        sort: sort,
        price_min: price_min,
        price_max: price_max,
        province: province,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Scrape one 1688.com offer's full detail.
    #
    # Fetches one 1688.com offer (by `offer_id` or `url`) and returns it as JSON: `title`,
    # `status`, `brand`, `category`, prices in yuan (`currency` CNY: `priceText`,
    # `priceMin`/`priceMax`), `pricing` (`tiers` when every SKU is priced by the quantity ladder
    # `priceTiers`, `sku` when each SKU carries its own `price`), `originalPriceTiers` (before a
    # promotion), `unit`, `moq` (minimum order), `available` (stock), `sold` + `soldText` +
    # `soldPeriod`, `variantOptions` (option names and values with images) and `variants` (every
    # SKU with `skuId`, `options`, `price`, `available`), `attributes`, `images`, `video`,
    # `descriptionUrl`, `shipping` (`from`, `dispatch` promise, `unitWeightKg`, `freeShipping`),
    # `services` (guarantees), `labels`, `rating` (`goodRatePercent`, `score`, `reviewCount`,
    # `reviewsWithPhotos`, review `tags`), `favorites` and the `supplier` (`name`, `loginId`,
    # `memberId`, `userId`, `shopUrl`, `serviceScore`, `repeatPurchaseRate3m`, `factory`,
    # `tpMember`, `location`). Text is returned in Chinese as 1688 publishes it. Companion to
    # `/marketplace/1688-search`.
    #
    # @param offer_id [String] Numeric 1688 offer id, e.g. '735353578254' (the number in
    # detail.1688.com/offer/<id>.html).
    # @param url [String] 1688 offer link, e.g.
    # 'https://detail.1688.com/offer/735353578254.html' (mobile m.1688.com and offerId= links
    # work too). Either offer_id or url is required.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'DE',
    # 'SG'). Leave blank to let the API pick.
    # Calls POST /marketplace/1688-product.
    def alibaba1688_product(offer_id = nil, url: nil, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/1688-product", {
        offer_id: offer_id,
        url: url,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Scrape Wish product search.
    #
    # Searches Wish (wish.com) for `query` and returns `products`: `id`, `name`, `url`, `price`,
    # `originalPrice` (crossed-out price, when discounted), `currency`, `priceText`, `priceUsd`
    # (Wish's USD value, comparable across markets), `shipping`, `rating`, `ratingCount`,
    # `numBought`, `inventory`, `colors`, `sizes`, `merchant` (`id`, `name`, `rating`,
    # `ratingCount`, `feedback`, `country`), `originCountry`, `shipsFrom`, `tileText`,
    # `isWishPick`, `position`, `image` and `thumbnail`, plus `totalResults` and `nextPage`.
    # Wish shows the catalogue and prices of the request's country (`proxy_country`, default
    # US). Collects up to `max_results` from `page` on, billed one unit per page.
    #
    # @param query [String] What to search for, e.g. 'yoga mat' or 'phone case', or a
    # wish.com/search/... link.
    # @param page [Integer] 1-based results page to start from (1-300, up to 30 products per
    # page). API default: 1.
    # @param max_results [Integer] Products to collect across pages, 1-300. Each page fetched is
    # billed one unit. API default: 30.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'GB', 'DE'). Wish shows the catalogue, prices and currency of that country. Default 'US'
    # (prices in USD).
    # Calls POST /marketplace/wish-search.
    def wish_search(query, page: nil, max_results: nil, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/wish-search", {
        query: query,
        page: page,
        max_results: max_results,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Scrape one Wish product.
    #
    # One Wish (wish.com) product as JSON: `id`, `name`, `url`, `price` (cheapest available
    # variant), `originalPrice`, `currency`, `priceUsd`, `priceRange`, `shipping`, `inStock`,
    # `rating`, `ratingCount`, `description`, `attributes`, `badges`, `images`, `merchant`
    # (`id`, `name`, `handle`, `rating`, `ratingCount`, `tier`), `shipsFrom`, `shipsTo`,
    # `deliveryEstimate`, `returnPolicy`, `variants` (`id`, `color`, `size`, `price`,
    # `originalPrice`, `priceUsd`, `shipping`, `inventory`, `available`) and `topReviews`
    # (`rating`, `comment`, `date`, `variant`, `upvotes`, `country`; no reviewer names). Prices
    # are those of the request's country (`proxy_country`, default US). One unit per call.
    #
    # @param product [String] A Wish product id ('5f96ad46b3f6480c7b9d7b52') or a product link
    # (https://www.wish.com/product/..., /c/...).
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'GB', 'DE'). Wish shows the catalogue, prices and currency of that country. Default 'US'
    # (prices in USD).
    # Calls POST /marketplace/wish-product.
    def wish_product(product, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/wish-product", {
        product: product,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Search TikTok Shop products by keyword or category.
    #
    # Lists TikTok Shop (US) products for a keyword (`q`) or a category (`category`, URL or id).
    # Each product card carries `productId`, `url`, `title`, `image`, `price` (current,
    # original, discountPercent, currency, fromPrice), `rating`, `reviewCount`, `soldCount`,
    # `brand`, `seller` (id, name, logo), promotion `labels` and, when TikTok binds one, the
    # promoting `video` (id, url, author, play and like counts, `durationSeconds`). A keyword
    # search also returns `relatedSearches` and `relatedCategories`; a category returns its
    # `subcategories` and `breadcrumbs`. Up to 30 products (one page, one billed request). A
    # keyword or category TikTok has no listing for returns 404.
    #
    # @param q [String] Search keyword, e.g. 'led face mask' (or a TikTok Shop keyword URL like
    # 'https://www.tiktok.com/shop/product/led-face-mask'). Either this or `category`.
    # @param category [String] List a category instead of a keyword: a category URL
    # ('https://www.tiktok.com/shop/c/beauty-personal-care/601450') or its numeric id
    # ('601450').
    # @param max_results [Integer] Products to return (1-30). One page is read: a keyword lists
    # up to 30 products, a category about 15. API default: 30.
    # Calls POST /social/tiktok-shop-search.
    def tiktok_shop_search(q = nil, category: nil, max_results: nil)
      post_json("/social/tiktok-shop-search", {
        q: q,
        category: category,
        max_results: max_results,
      })
    end

    # Scrape one TikTok Shop product.
    #
    # Fetches a public TikTok Shop (US) product page by `url` or `product_id` and returns it as
    # JSON: `productId`, `url`, `title`, `description` (plus `descriptionImages`), `status`,
    # `available`, `brand`, `price` (current, original, discountPercent, currency, display
    # strings, min/max for a price range), `soldCount`, `rating`, `reviewCount`,
    # `ratingDistribution`, `categories`, `images`, `options` and `variants` (per-SKU price,
    # stock and availability), `specifications`, `shipping` (fee, free, delivery days and
    # estimate), promotion `labels`, `seller` (id, name, store URL, rating, followers, sold
    # count, product / video / review counts, service scores, business name and address) and the
    # top `reviews` the page shows (rating, text, date, variant, images). One billed request. No
    # login or cookies; a product that does not exist or is not sold in the US returns 404.
    #
    # @param url [String] A TikTok Shop product URL ('https://www.tiktok.com/shop/pdp/goli-
    # ashwagandha/1729527313880355335', 'https://shop.tiktok.com/us/pdp/1729527313880355335', a
    # /view/product/ link) or a bare product id. Either this or `product_id`.
    # @param product_id [String] The numeric product id (e.g. '1729527313880355335').
    # Calls POST /social/tiktok-shop-product.
    def tiktok_shop_product(url = nil, product_id: nil)
      post_json("/social/tiktok-shop-product", {
        url: url,
        product_id: product_id,
      })
    end

    # Scrape a TikTok Shop store and its products.
    #
    # Fetches a TikTok Shop (US) store by URL or seller id and returns its profile as `store`
    # (id, name, url, rating, followers, soldCount, productCount, reviewCount, videoCount, logo,
    # label such as 'OFFICIAL SHOP', service `scores` like positive feedback and on-time
    # delivery, description) plus the `products` on its storefront page (up to 20, same card
    # shape as /social/tiktok-shop-search) and `hasMore`. The store page does not carry the
    # seller's business name and address, so `businessName` / `businessAddress` are null here; a
    # product's `seller` (/social/tiktok-shop-product) has them. A store with no products listed
    # returns its profile and an empty `products`. One billed request. Most stores answer in a
    # few seconds; a store TikTok shows only past its verification puzzle (common for smaller
    # shops) is read through that puzzle and can take up to about 50 s. A seller id TikTok has
    # no US store for returns 404.
    #
    # @param store [String] A TikTok Shop store URL ('https://www.tiktok.com/shop/store/goli-
    # nutrition/7495794203056835079') or the seller id ('7495794203056835079').
    # @param max_results [Integer] Storefront products to return (0-20); 0 = store profile only.
    # One page is read. API default: 20.
    # Calls POST /social/tiktok-shop-store.
    def tiktok_shop_store(store, max_results: nil)
      post_json("/social/tiktok-shop-store", {
        store: store,
        max_results: max_results,
      })
    end

    # Scrape Shopee product search.
    #
    # Searches a Shopee market (Singapore, Indonesia, Malaysia, Thailand, Vietnam, Philippines,
    # Taiwan or Brazil - `country`) for `q` and returns one page of results: up to 40
    # `products`, each with `position`, `itemId`, `shopId`, `name`, `url`, `image`, `price`,
    # `originalPrice` (when Shopee shows the crossed-out price), `discountPercent`, `currency`,
    # `rating` (average stars), `location` (where the seller ships from) and `labels` (promotion
    # badges). `sort` orders the results, `min_price` / `max_price` filter them, `shop_id` keeps
    # one shop's products (or lists the shop without `q`), and `url` takes a Shopee search or
    # category link instead. Shopee shows one page per search, so run several sort orders or
    # price ranges for more products. `price` is what Shopee shows a signed-out shopper, which
    # can be a promotional or new-customer price (see `labels`). Not available: stock, units
    # sold, rating counts and reviews (Shopee does not publish them on the pages these endpoints
    # read). One unit per call.
    #
    # @param q [String] What to search for, e.g. 'iphone case' or 'air fryer'. Optional with
    # `shop_id`.
    # @param country [String] Shopee market: 'sg' (shopee.sg), 'id' (shopee.co.id), 'my'
    # (shopee.com.my), 'th' (shopee.co.th), 'vn' (shopee.vn), 'ph' (shopee.ph), 'tw'
    # (shopee.tw), 'br' (shopee.com.br). Default 'sg'. Prices are in that market's currency.
    # @param shop_id [String] Only this shop's products (the number in a shop's links, e.g.
    # 442800909). Without `q` it lists the shop.
    # @param url [String] A Shopee search or category link (e.g.
    # https://shopee.sg/search?keyword=lego or https://shopee.sg/Cases-Covers-
    # cat.11013350.11013434.11027839), used as it is; `q`, `country`, `shop_id`, `sort` and the
    # price filters are then ignored.
    # @param sort [String] Result order: relevance, sales, newest, price_asc, price_desc. API
    # default: relevance.
    # @param min_price [Integer] Lowest price, in the market's currency.
    # @param max_price [Integer] Highest price, in the market's currency.
    # @param max_results [Integer] Products to return, 1-40 (one Shopee results page). API
    # default: 40.
    # Calls POST /marketplace/shopee-search.
    def shopee_search(q = nil, country: nil, shop_id: nil, url: nil, sort: nil, min_price: nil, max_price: nil, max_results: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/shopee-search", {
        q: q,
        country: country,
        shop_id: shop_id,
        url: url,
        sort: sort,
        min_price: min_price,
        max_price: max_price,
        max_results: max_results,
      })
    end

    # Scrape one Shopee product.
    #
    # One Shopee product as JSON, from a product link (`url`) or `shop_id` + `item_id` +
    # `country`: `title`, `price`, `originalPrice`, `discountPercent`, `currency`, `rating`
    # (average stars), `labels`, `images`, `shopLocation` and `shop` (`name`, `username`, `url`,
    # `rating`, `ratingCount`, `followers`, `itemCount`, `responseRatePercent`,
    # `isOfficialShop`, `isPreferredPlusSeller`, `location`, `joinedAt`). With `dataLevel: full`
    # it also has `description`, `brand`, `condition`, `categories`, `videos`, `variations`
    # (option names), `models` (`modelId`, `name`), `attributes`, `isOfficialShop`,
    # `isPreOrder`, `estimatedShippingDays` and `createdAt`; `dataLevel: meta` means Shopee
    # showed only the product's title and main image (some markets), with price, rating and shop
    # still included. `price` is what Shopee shows a signed-out shopper, which can be a
    # promotional or new-customer price (see `labels`). Not available: stock, units sold, rating
    # counts and reviews (Shopee does not publish them on the pages these endpoints read). One
    # unit per call.
    #
    # @param url [String] A Shopee product link, e.g. https://shopee.sg/Beats-
    # iPhone-17-Case-i.442800909.40270108836 or
    # https://shopee.co.id/product/1426163997/40581375446.
    # @param shop_id [String] Instead of `url`: the shop id (the first number after '-i.' in a
    # product link).
    # @param item_id [String] Instead of `url`: the item id (the second number after '-i.').
    # @param country [String] With `shop_id` + `item_id`: Shopee market: 'sg' (shopee.sg), 'id'
    # (shopee.co.id), 'my' (shopee.com.my), 'th' (shopee.co.th), 'vn' (shopee.vn), 'ph'
    # (shopee.ph), 'tw' (shopee.tw), 'br' (shopee.com.br). Default 'sg'. Prices are in that
    # market's currency.
    # Calls POST /marketplace/shopee-product.
    def shopee_product(url = nil, shop_id: nil, item_id: nil, country: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/shopee-product", {
        url: url,
        shop_id: shop_id,
        item_id: item_id,
        country: country,
      })
    end

    # Scrape Taobao / Tmall keyword or category listings.
    #
    # Returns the products Taobao lists for a keyword `q` (or a `category`) as JSON: `products`
    # (`position`, `itemId`, `title`, `url`, `image`, `price` in yuan with `currency` CNY,
    # `priceLabel` (Taobao's price tag, e.g. 优惠价), `localPrices` (the same price in the
    # storefront's currency, HKD and TWD), `shopId`, `shopName`, `descriptionMatchScore`,
    # `freeShipping`, `categoryId`, `rootCategoryId`, `sellingPoints`, `reviewHighlights`),
    # `totalResults` (how many listings Taobao reports), and `filterOptions` (brand and property
    # facets; pass an option's `filter` value back as `filter`). Sort by relevance, sales or
    # price and filter by a yuan price range (products whose listed price falls outside it are
    # left out and counted in `droppedOutsidePriceRange`). Taobao shows signed-out visitors only
    # the first 20 products of a list, so one call returns up to 20 (narrow with price ranges
    # and filters to reach more). When Taobao has no list for the keyword, the call answers with
    # the list of the closest keyword Taobao itself suggests and says so: `keywordSubstituted`
    # true and `matchedKeyword`. Text comes in Chinese as sellers write it. Companion to
    # `/marketplace/taobao-product`. One unit per call.
    #
    # @param q [String] Keyword, in Chinese or English, e.g. '手机壳', '连衣裙', 'phone case' (Chinese
    # keywords match far more listings). A Taobao search or list link works too. Give `q` or
    # `category`.
    # @param category [String] A Taobao category id, e.g. '50005050', or a category list link
    # (https://www.taobao.com/list/category/50005050.htm). Returns the category's best sellers;
    # sort and filters apply to keyword searches only.
    # @param sort [String] Order: relevance, sales, price_asc, price_desc (price in yuan). API
    # default: relevance.
    # @param price_min [Float] Only products at or above this many yuan (CNY).
    # @param price_max [Float] Only products at or below this many yuan (CNY).
    # @param filter [String] One brand or property filter, as the `filter` value of an option in
    # `filterOptions` of an earlier answer, e.g. '20000-88634403'.
    # Calls POST /marketplace/taobao-search.
    def taobao_search(q = nil, category: nil, sort: nil, price_min: nil, price_max: nil, filter: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/taobao-search", {
        q: q,
        category: category,
        sort: sort,
        price_min: price_min,
        price_max: price_max,
        filter: filter,
      })
    end

    # Scrape one Taobao / Tmall item.
    #
    # Returns one Taobao or Tmall item (by `item_id` or `url`) as JSON: `itemId`, `url`,
    # `platform` (taobao / tmall), `title` (`titleTruncated` when Taobao shortens it, as it does
    # for Tmall items), `price`, `originalPrice` and `priceMax` (for a price range) in yuan with
    # `currency` CNY, `image`, `location` (ships from), `categoryId`, `rootCategoryId`,
    # `categoryPath`, `freeShipping`, `paymentMethods`, `sellableLanguages`, `rating` (positive
    # / neutral / negative split and counts; Taobao items only, Tmall does not publish it),
    # `latestReview` (`rating`, `content`, `date`, `variant`, `hasMedia`, `followUps`; no
    # reviewer identity, so no review photo or video URLs) and `shop` (`shopId`, `name`, `url`,
    # `logo`, `sellerType` B = Tmall / C = Taobao, `creditLevel`, `openedAt`, `itemCount`,
    # `scores` for description, service and delivery). This is what Taobao shows signed-out
    # visitors: variants (SKUs), stock and monthly sales need a Taobao login and are not
    # included. Companion to `/marketplace/taobao-search`. One unit per call.
    #
    # @param item_id [String] Numeric Taobao or Tmall item id, e.g. '765833709683' (the `id` in
    # item.taobao.com/item.htm?id=...).
    # @param url [String] Taobao or Tmall item link, e.g.
    # 'https://item.taobao.com/item.htm?id=765833709683' or
    # 'https://detail.tmall.com/item.htm?id=1081364414020' (world.taobao.com, mobile and
    # overseas item links work too). Either item_id or url is required.
    # Calls POST /marketplace/taobao-product.
    def taobao_product(item_id = nil, url: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/taobao-product", {
        item_id: item_id,
        url: url,
      })
    end

    # Scrape Vinted product search.
    #
    # Searches Vinted for `query` and returns the listings as JSON: `title`, `price` and
    # `currency`, `brand`, `size`, `condition`, `image` and an item `url`. Pick the marketplace
    # with `domain`, sort with `order`, filter with `price_from`/`price_to`, and collect up to
    # `max_results` across pages.
    #
    # @param query [String] What to search, e.g. 'nike air max' or 'levis 501'.
    # @param domain [String] Marketplace TLD: co.uk, com, de, fr, it, es, nl, pl. API default:
    # co.uk.
    # @param order [String] Ordering: relevance, newest_first, price_low_to_high,
    # price_high_to_low. API default: relevance.
    # @param price_from [Integer] Lowest price to include.
    # @param price_to [Integer] Highest price to include.
    # @param max_results [Integer] How many listings to collect across pages. API default: 96.
    # @param page [Integer] 1-based page to start from (~96 per page). API default: 1.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'DE'). Defaults to an EU country.
    # Calls POST /marketplace/vinted-search.
    def vinted_search(query, domain: nil, order: nil, price_from: nil, price_to: nil, max_results: nil, page: nil, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/vinted-search", {
        query: query,
        domain: domain,
        order: order,
        price_from: price_from,
        price_to: price_to,
        max_results: max_results,
        page: page,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Scrape Leboncoin search.
    #
    # Searches Leboncoin (France) for `query` and returns the ads as JSON: `id`, `title`,
    # `price` and `currency`, `location` (city + postcode), `category`, publication `date`,
    # `image`, listing `url`, `sellerType` (pro/private) and the ad's `attributes`. Narrow with
    # `category`, `location` and `min_price`/`max_price`, order with `sort`, and collect up to
    # `max_results` across pages. Paid 'a la une' placements (`sponsored: true`) are left out
    # unless `include_sponsored=true`.
    #
    # @param query [String] What to search, e.g. 'velo electrique' or 'iphone 13'.
    # @param category [String] Category: vehicles, cars, motorcycles, vans, car_parts,
    # real_estate, real_estate_sale, rentals, flatshare, holiday_rentals, commercial_property,
    # electronics, computers, photo_audio_video, phones, consoles, video_games,
    # computer_accessories, home_garden, furniture, appliances, diy, decoration, garden,
    # fashion, clothing, shoes, bags_accessories, watches_jewelry, baby_equipment, leisure,
    # books, sports, bikes, toys, music_instruments, collectibles, antiques, animals, jobs,
    # job_offers, or a numeric Leboncoin category id.
    # @param location [String] Where to search: a city ('Bordeaux'), a city with postcode
    # ('Toulouse 31000'), a department code ('75') or a region ('Ile-de-France').
    # @param min_price [Integer] Lowest price to include (EUR).
    # @param max_price [Integer] Highest price to include (EUR).
    # @param sort [String] Ordering: relevance, newest, price_low, price_high. API default:
    # relevance.
    # @param max_results [Integer] How many listings to collect across pages. API default: 35.
    # @param page [Integer] 1-based page to start from (35 per page). API default: 1.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'DE'). Optional.
    # @param include_sponsored [Boolean] Also return Leboncoin's paid 'a la une' placements
    # (`sponsored: true`). Off by default: they ignore the query, category and sort. API
    # default: false.
    # Calls POST /marketplace/leboncoin-search.
    def leboncoin_search(query, category: nil, location: nil, min_price: nil, max_price: nil, sort: nil, max_results: nil, page: nil, proxy_country: nil, include_sponsored: nil)
      post_json("/marketplace/leboncoin-search", {
        query: query,
        category: category,
        location: location,
        min_price: min_price,
        max_price: max_price,
        sort: sort,
        max_results: max_results,
        page: page,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
        include_sponsored: include_sponsored,
      })
    end

    # Scrape Woolworths (Australia) groceries.
    #
    # Woolworths Australia (woolworths.com.au) products as JSON. `mode=search&query=`,
    # `mode=category&category=` and `mode=specials` return `products`: `id` (stockcode), `name`,
