    # returns its profile: `name`, `tagline`, `description`, `website` and social links,
    # `companySize`, `stage`, `badges`, `markets`, `locations`, `companyTypes`, `hiring`,
    # `openJobs` with `openJobsByRole`, `totalRaised`, `fundingRounds` (`type`, `date`,
    # `valuation`), `founders` (name, profile URL, role, bio, location), `teamMembersCount`,
    # `perks`, `media`, the first open `jobs` (with `jobsTotal`) and `similarCompanies`. Company
    # profiles sit behind a Cloudflare challenge, so a call can take up to about a minute.
    # `mode=search` lists Wellfound's startup directory by `location` or `industry` (10
    # companies per page, paged up to `max_results`) with website, description, markets,
    # locations and open-job counts. Billed one unit per page fetched (`pagesFetched`).
    #
    # @param company [String] mode=profile: the company slug ('stripe') or URL
    # (https://wellfound.com/company/stripe).
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'DE'). Leave blank for the country chosen for the site.
    # Calls POST /companies/wellfound.
    def wellfound_company(company, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/companies/wellfound", {
        mode: "profile",
        company: company,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Scrape Wellfound startup company profiles.
    #
    # Given a Wellfound `company` (slug like `stripe` or a wellfound.com/company/<slug> URL),
    # returns its profile: `name`, `tagline`, `description`, `website` and social links,
    # `companySize`, `stage`, `badges`, `markets`, `locations`, `companyTypes`, `hiring`,
    # `openJobs` with `openJobsByRole`, `totalRaised`, `fundingRounds` (`type`, `date`,
