    # month change as a fraction: 0.069 = +6.9%, -0.2 = -20%), `technology`, `predictions`,
    # `events` (product launches, partnerships, awards, layoffs, key employee changes, legal
    # proceedings, each with its press source), `offices` and recent `news`. Every one of the
    # record's 73 keys is always present. Data Crunchbase shows only to paying users (founded /
    # closed / IPO dates, funding totals, round dates and amounts, acquisition prices, exits,
    # valuation) is null, and `paywalledFields` names the ones Crunchbase holds for this
    # organization. With `query` instead, searches organizations by name and returns up to
    # `max_results` (max 25) matches with `name`, `slug`, `url`, `shortDescription` and `logo`,
    # plus the total `count` of matches. No Crunchbase login required.
