    # ('310633997'), 'id310633997', an apps.apple.com app URL, or a bundle id
    # ('net.whatsapp.WhatsApp').
    # @param country [String] App Store country (ISO-2), e.g. 'us', 'gb', 'de'. Prices, ratings
    # and reviews are per country. Default: the country in an app URL, else 'us'.
    # @param max_results [Integer] mode=search: apps to return (1-200). mode=reviews: reviews to
    # collect (1-500); Apple serves 50 per page and at most 10 pages per country, each page
    # billed as one request. API default: 50.
    # @param sort [String] Review order for mode=reviews: mostrecent, mosthelpful. API default:
    # mostrecent.
    # @param page [Integer] mode=reviews: review page to start from (1-10). Use `nextPage` of a
    # previous response to continue. When the last page was only partly used, `nextPage` points
    # at it again, so skip reviews whose `id` you already have. API default: 1.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'DE'). Leave blank to let the API pick.
    # Calls POST /apps/app-store.
    def app_store_reviews(app_id, country: nil, max_results: nil, sort: nil, page: nil, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/apps/app-store", {
        mode: "reviews",
        app_id: app_id,
        country: country,
        max_results: max_results,
        sort: sort,
        page: page,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Scrape a YouTube channel's videos.
    #
    # Returns a YouTube channel's recent videos as JSON: `videoId`, `title`, `views`,
    # `published`, `thumbnail` and a watch `url`, plus a `channel` summary (name, id). Pass a
    # handle (`@mkbhd`), a channel id (`UC...`) or a channel URL. Returns the channel's first
    # page of videos (about 30).
    #
    # @param channel [String] Channel handle (@mkbhd), channel id (UC...) or a channel URL.
    # @param tab [String] Which tab: videos, shorts, streams. API default: videos.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'DE').
    # @param limit [Integer] Max videos to return (1-200). Honoured on the 'videos' tab; other
    # tabs return a single scraped page. API default: 30.
    # Calls POST /content/youtube-channel.
    def youtube_channel(channel, tab: nil, proxy_country: nil, limit: nil)
      post_json("/content/youtube-channel", {
        channel: channel,
        tab: tab,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
        limit: limit,
      })
    end

    # Search YouTube.
    #
    # Searches YouTube for `query` and returns the results as JSON. For each video: `videoId`,
    # `title`, `url`, `channel` (name/id/url), `publishedText`, `viewCount` (+ text),
    # `lengthSeconds` (+ text), `thumbnails`, `descriptionSnippet`, `badges`, `verified` and
    # `isLive`. Filter with `type` (video / channel / playlist / all) and `sort` (relevance /
    # date / views / rating), and collect up to `max_results` across pages.
    #
    # @param query [String] Search terms.
    # @param max_results [Integer] How many results to collect across pages (~20 per page). API
    # default: 20.
    # @param type [String] Result type: video, channel, playlist, movie, all. API default:
    # video.
    # @param sort [String] Ordering: relevance, rating, date, views. API default: relevance.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'DE'). Defaults to US.
    # Calls POST /content/youtube-search.
    def youtube_search(query, max_results: nil, type: nil, sort: nil, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/content/youtube-search", {
        query: query,
        max_results: max_results,
        type: type,
        sort: sort,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Get a YouTube video transcript.
    #
    # Returns a YouTube video's captions as JSON: timestamped `segments` (`start`, `dur`,
    # `text`) and a joined `text`, plus `availableLanguages`, the picked `language`,
    # `isAutoGenerated`, and the video's `title`, `author` and `lengthSeconds`. Pass a video id
    # or any YouTube video URL; choose a caption language with `lang`. Ideal for LLM/RAG
    # pipelines, subtitles and content analysis.
    #
    # @param video [String] Video id (dQw4w9WgXcQ) or any YouTube video URL.
    # @param lang [String] Preferred caption language code, e.g. 'en'. Omit for the
    # default/first track. A prefix like 'en' matches 'en-US'.
    # @param format [String] Output shape: text, segments. 'segments' returns timestamps; 'text'
    # returns only the joined plaintext. API default: segments.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'DE') for the watch page. Defaults to US.
    # Calls POST /content/youtube-transcript.
    def youtube_transcript(video, lang: nil, format: nil, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/content/youtube-transcript", {
        video: video,
        lang: lang,
        format: format,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Scrape Spotify artists, albums, tracks, playlists and search.
    #
    # Returns Spotify catalog data as JSON, including the play counts and audience numbers the
    # official Web API does not expose. `type=artist`: `artist` (`followers`,
    # `monthlyListeners`, `worldRank`, `topCities`, `biography`, `externalLinks`, images,
    # `verified`), `topTracks` with `playcount` (a top track's `album` carries `name` and
    # `releaseDate` when Spotify lists that album among the artist's releases), `discography`
    # groups (popular releases, albums, singles, compilations with totals), `relatedArtists`,
    # `appearsOn`, `featuredOn` / `discoveredOn` playlists; `discography=true` adds the full
    # `releases` list, paged. `type=album`: `album` (type, release date, label, copyright,
    # artists, cover) and `tracks` with `playcount`, paged. `type=track`: `track` with
    # `playcount`, duration, explicit flag, album and every credited artist. `type=playlist`:
    # `playlist` (name, description, `followers`, owner, cover, `totalTracks`) and `tracks` with
    # `playcount`, `addedAt`, `bpm` and `key`, paged. `type=search&query=`: `results` of
    # `search_type` tracks, artists, albums or playlists, paged; a search with no match answers
    # 200 with empty `results`. `playcount` comes only on artist, album, track and playlist
    # lookups: Spotify's search does not return it, so search track results have no `playcount`
    # key (look a track up with `type=track` for its count). `id` takes an open.spotify.com URL,
    # a Spotify URI or a bare id. Lists page with `offset` / `max_results` and answer `hasMore`
    # / `nextOffset`; each page fetched is one billed unit (`pagesFetched`).
    #
    # @param query [String] Search text for type=search, e.g. 'daft punk'.
    # @param search_type [String] What a search returns: tracks, artists, albums, playlists. API
    # default: tracks.
    # @param offset [Integer] 0-based position to start from in the list being paged: album
    # tracks, playlist tracks, search results, or the full discography with discography=true.
    # Use the `nextOffset` of a previous response to continue. Spotify serves search results up
    # to position 1000. API default: 0.
    # @param max_results [Integer] How many list items to collect. Album tracks: 1-1000 (default
    # 100, 100 per page). Playlist tracks: 1-2000 (default 100, 100 per page). Search: 1-1000
    # (default 20, 50 per page). Artist releases with discography=true: 1-1000 (default 50, 50
    # per page). Each page fetched is one billed unit.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'DE', 'GB').
    # Spotify's market follows it, which can change `playable` and search order; play counts are
    # the same everywhere. Leave blank for any.
    # Calls POST /music/spotify.
    def spotify_search(query, search_type: nil, offset: nil, max_results: nil, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/music/spotify", {
        type: "search",
        query: query,
        search_type: search_type,
        offset: offset,
        max_results: max_results,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

