    # Get a website's Similarweb traffic overview.
    #
    # Returns Similarweb's public traffic overview for `domain` as JSON: `globalRank`,
    # `countryRank` (with `country`), `categoryRank` (with `category`) and their month-over-
    # month changes; `totalVisits` for the latest month with `visitsChangePercent`;
    # `bounceRate`, `pagesPerVisit`, `avgVisitDuration`/`avgVisitDurationSeconds`;
    # `visitsHistory` (the last 3 months - earlier months are derived from Similarweb's own
    # month-over-month change) and `rankHistory`; `trafficSources` (channel shares -
    # Similarweb's free page reveals only some, the rest are null); `topCountries`;
    # `demographics` (gender, age groups); `competitors` (similar sites with affinity); `search`
    # (organic/paid split and top keywords); `socialNetworks`, `referrals`, `outgoingLinks`,
    # `displayAds`; `technologies`; `audienceInterests`; and the `company` profile.
    # `snapshotDate` is the month the data describes. A domain Similarweb has no page for
    # returns `found: false` with the same keys set to null/empty; a known domain too small to
    # estimate returns `hasTrafficData: false`.
    #
    # @param domain [String] Website to look up: a bare domain ('github.com'), a URL
    # ('https://www.github.com/about'), or a Similarweb page URL. A leading 'www.' is dropped;
    # other subdomains ('docs.python.org') are kept.
    # @param proxy_country [String] Proxy country the request is sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US',
    # 'DE'). Optional.
    # Calls POST /seo/similarweb.
    def similarweb_overview(domain, proxy_country: nil)
      post_json("/seo/similarweb", {
        domain: domain,
        proxy_country: proxy_country,
      })
    end

    # Run Ahrefs' free SEO tools (DR, backlinks, traffic, keywords, KD, SERP).
    #
    # Ahrefs' free SEO tools as JSON, without an Ahrefs account.
    # `tool=authority&target=<domain>`: `domainRating`, `backlinks`, `referringDomains`,
    # `dofollowBacklinksPercent`, `dofollowReferringDomainsPercent`. `tool=backlinks`: the same
    # plus `topBacklinks` (`urlFrom`, `urlTo`, `title`, `anchor`, `textBefore`/`textAfter`,
    # `domainRating`). `tool=traffic`: `organicTraffic`, `trafficValueUsd`, `trafficHistory`,
    # `topPages`, `topCountries`, `topKeywords` (`country` narrows it to one market).
    # `tool=broken-links`: `inbound` broken backlinks and `outbound` broken links on the site's
    # pages. `tool=keyword-difficulty&keyword=<phrase>`: `difficulty` (0-100),
    # `referringDomainsToRank` and the SERP `results`. `tool=keywords`: `ideas` and
    # `questionIdeas` with `difficulty` and `volume` buckets, plus totals (Google). `tool=serp`:
    # the top Google `results` (organic with `metrics` - DR, UR, backlinks, referring domains,
    # traffic, value, keywords - plus AI overview, questions, shopping, local and news blocks).
    # Domain tools take `mode` (subdomains, domain, prefix, exact). One call, one unit.
    #
    # @param tool [String] Which Ahrefs free tool to run: 'authority' (Domain Rating),
    # 'backlinks', 'traffic', 'broken-links' (these take `target`), 'keyword-difficulty',
    # 'keywords' (keyword ideas), 'serp' (these take `keyword`).
    # @param target [String] Domain or URL for the domain tools, e.g. 'github.com' or
    # 'https://github.com/features'.
    # @param keyword [String] Search phrase for the keyword tools, e.g. 'running shoes'.
    # @param country [String] Two-letter market code. Keyword tools: the search market (default
    # 'us'). traffic: limits the estimate to that country (default: worldwide). Not used by the
    # other domain tools.
    # @param mode [String] Target scope for the domain tools: 'subdomains' (the domain with all
    # its subdomains), 'domain' (without subdomains), 'prefix' (everything under the URL) or
    # 'exact' (that URL only). API default: subdomains.
    # @param protocol [String] traffic only: 'both', 'http' or 'https'. API default: both.
    # @param questions [Boolean] keywords only: also return question ideas. API default: true.
    # Calls POST /seo/ahrefs.
    def ahrefs(tool, target: nil, keyword: nil, country: nil, mode: nil, protocol: nil, questions: nil)
      post_json("/seo/ahrefs", {
        tool: tool,
        target: target,
        keyword: keyword,
        country: country,
        mode: mode,
        protocol: protocol,
        questions: questions,
      })
    end

    # Get a website's Semrush overview (Authority Score, traffic, backlinks).
    #
    # Semrush's public website data for `domain`, without a Semrush account. `report=overview`
    # (default): `authorityScore`, `globalRank`, `countryRank`, `categoryRank`, `visits` with
    # `visitsChangePercent` and `visitsHistory` (desktop/mobile), `pagesPerVisit`,
    # `timeOnSiteSeconds`, `bounceRate`, `searchTraffic` (organic and paid with history),
    # `backlinks` (backlinks, referring domains, Google penalty risk, history), `topKeywords`
    # (position, search volume, CPC, traffic share, intent), `topCountries`, `competitors`,
    # `trafficSources` (incoming and outgoing) and `aiTraffic` (visits from AI assistants).
    # `report=competitors`: the domain's competitors, each with Authority Score, ranks, visits
    # and engagement. Semrush publishes these pages for about 200k of the most visited sites;
    # any other domain returns `found: false`. One call, one unit.
    #
    # @param domain [String] Website to look up: a domain ('github.com'), a URL
    # ('https://www.github.com/about') or a Semrush website page URL. A leading 'www.' is
    # dropped; other subdomains are kept.
    # @param report [String] 'overview' (traffic, rank, search traffic, backlinks, keywords,
    # countries, competitors, sources) or 'competitors' (the competitor list with each one's
    # ranks, visits and engagement). API default: overview.
    # Calls POST /seo/semrush.
    def semrush_overview(domain, report: nil)
      post_json("/seo/semrush", {
        domain: domain,
        report: report,
      })
    end

    private

    def plugin_join(value, sep)
      value.is_a?(Array) ? value.join(sep) : value
    end
  end
end
